{"title":"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For each non-zero real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, we define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/5/f654b1b0ac7586033bb135ae89efcd53934d20d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{*} = \\frac{5}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/9/fa9e61e29759876170023f48f8f62a1987d15042.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(100^{*})^{*}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" /> is equal to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/3/6b36b050cdae88253c9d8dd676f933ab8c1b6d5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 100 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ \\frac{1}{4} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 20 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ \\frac{1}{20} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ \\frac{1}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"454\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3de91fa93082e16f622a49524dca35e337067ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100^{*}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/5/5950f20b6fc68d1aee0ba8a81181cc6f3ce05c08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Next, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/2/4b2b2aab078565181fb297226b04099f3d062478.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{5}{100})^{*}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"55\" height=\"38\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/9/b79b65c18e56d505313e99e5c5060622d22e8b99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{\\frac{5}{100}} = \\frac{5 \\times 100}{5} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } 100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"215\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28general.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(general)\">Solution 2 (general)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (general)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In general, for any value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, we see that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/f/9afc39134e8a2e3954ce41ab445a01a38b6dcfd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^{*})^{*} = (\\frac{5}{a})^{*} = \\frac{5}{\\frac{5}{a}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"140\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/5/05504b2ab4814e7d5e96379249c8b2e94639f397.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{5 \\times a}{5} = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"100\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Thus, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/3/c63da515ca43dfa8711d96bae444031a98d6e388.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/3/cd36e6558d7fa89aa5eaed905964fa8b120f2d09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^{*})^{*} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } 100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"139\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley\">2025 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 18 (page does not exist)\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Pr